      "content": "It sounds stressful, but you can certainly work on optimizing your daily performance. To start, consider keeping a simple journal or use a productivity app to track your tasks, deadlines, and how you're managing your time each day. Set clear, achievable goals and prioritize your tasks using the Eisenhower Box method to focus on what's most important. Additionally, try to reduce distractions, practice mindfulness or brief relaxation exercises to stay focused, and schedule regular short breaks to avoid burnout. Remember that continuous improvement is a process, and it's okay to handle small setbacks—they're part of becoming more efficient.",
